Please note that prior to lodging a complaint with the above authorities, you are first required to lodge a complaint with this FSP and 
only after confirmation by this FSP that they are unable to resolve the complaint may it be escalated to these authorities. 
 
We have established a written internal complaint resolution system with detailed procedures. Access to the Complaints Procedures 
and a copy of the complaint resolution system is available to clients at this office each day during office hours. Should you have any 
complaint, this must be submitted to us in writing and must contain all relevant information. Copies of all relevant documentation must 
be attached thereto. 
 
4.  Remuneration of the Financial Advisor 

Page 4 of 4 
Step: 1 of the Six-Step Financial Planning Process                                                                     Version 3.0 – 01 February 2022 
 
4.1   The financial advisor is an employee of Royal Square Financial  and is remunerated only by Royal Square Finanical. The     
primary method of remuneration is in commissions earned from third party product suppliers as seen on the first page, shared 
through a commission split between the company and the financial advisor. 
 
4.2  Commission on all life insurance policies, endowment polies and retirement policies and living annuities is regulated by law and 
is standardised regardless of the product supplier that is used. 
 
4.3  Commission on investments business ranges from 1.00% to 5.00% depending on the product supplier that the advisor places the 
investment business with and how much commission the advisor deems appropriate. The proposed commission on investment 
business is 3.00% for all new business. Royal Square Financial earns ongoing commission on all active investments and the 
advisor is responsible at all times to review investment placement. 
 
4.4 Consultation fees are charged at R1, 500 per hour  Time spent on Work 
    (a)  The mandatory annual review in Q1  - one hour 
    (b)  Financial Needs Analysis & Report   - two hours (minimum) 
    (c)  Financial Plan Implementation - two hour (minimum) 
    (d)  Ad-hoc Consultation  - one hour 
 
 
4.5 R500 monthly retainer for fees: This is an option where the client pays a fixed monthly debit order that allows for free 
consultations throughout the year as needed and by appointment (12-MONTH MINIMUM TERM).  
*   Advice fees are quoted excluding VAT. The totals INCLUSIVE of VAT are R1, 710 per hour or R570 per month. 
 
 
 
 
